{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH appeared.</b> A vision (mar'eh) is in every case a rank lower than prophecy; therefore it says: וּשְׁמִי ה׳ לֹא נוֹדַעְתִּי לָהֶם (Exodus 6:3)." "<b>I am El Shaddai.</b> I am He whose existence suffices for the act unique to Me — creation — in which no recipient-of-action is involved, and therefore the Creator, in His action, requires nothing besides Himself to exist. The opposite holds for every existent other than the Creator: no agent other than He acts unless there exists some recipient-of-action from it, and likewise no recipient is acted upon unless there exists some agent to act upon it. From this, a demonstrative proof compels the existence of the Creator, His unity, and the perfection of His action over every other agent, upon every contemplator. All this the blessed Elohim taught to the Patriarchs. However, the demonstrative cause regarding creation, which derives from the unique Name, He did not make known until Moses our teacher, as He said: וָאֵרָא … וּשְׁמִי ה׳ לֹא נוֹדַעְתִּי לָהֶם (Exodus 6:3)." "<b>Walk.</b> In every direction you turn, there." "<b>Before Me</b> — as one who looks to Me to know My ways, so far as is possible for you, in the manner of שִׁוִּיתִי ה׳ לְנֶגְדִּי תָּמִיד (Psalms 16:8)." "<b>And be whole.</b> Attain the perfection possible for the human species — הַשְׂכֵּל וְיָדוֹעַ אוֹתִי (Jeremiah 9:23) — through knowing My ways and likening yourself to Me so far as is possible for you. For the action of every existent indicates its form, as it says: הוֹדִיעֵנִי נָא אֶת דְּרָכֶיךָ וְאֵדָעֲךָ (Exodus 33:13). This is the ultimate perfection for the human species, and that intended by the blessed Elohim in creation, as it says: נַעֲשֶׂה אָדָם בְּצַלְמֵנוּ כִּדְמוּתֵנוּ (Genesis 1:26)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:28.811419371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}